{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Bread of the Face, before Him always.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): it is called 'face' (פנים) because it had faces looking this way and that, toward the sides of the House from here and from here, and its walls were upright against the edge of the table." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash it is called 'face' (פנים) because its thickness was a handbreadth, and so the Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: there is no 'face' (פנים) less than a handbreadth — it is written here, ״אל פני הכפורת״, and it is written there (Genesis 27): ״מאת פני יצחק אביו״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah it is called 'face' (פנים) on account of 'before Him always' (לפני תמיד), and the mystery of the פנים has already been explained in the verse ״לא יהיה לך״, and behold this is clear."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {1 "The prooftext 'אל פני הכפורת' (before the face of the cover) alludes to Exodus 25:20ff where the cherubim's faces are directed toward the cover; the word פנים there is linked to the measure of a handbreadth."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:04:21.311665468Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}